# Prompt release v2.3.1-operational

Prompt release: `v2.3.1-operational`
Eligibility release inherited from: `v2.3-eligibility-registered`
Schema version: `v2.2.1` (FROZEN; unchanged)
Validation protocol: `C-2.3`

## Active methodological state

- Stage 1 uses the registered broad eligibility threshold: a paper is eligible
  when it presents, proposes, evaluates, or critiques an EnPI/EnB model with
  enough detail to identify and characterise it. Validation is an extracted
  variable, never an eligibility gate.
- Corpus-B classification uses the closed sector list and production mode.
  Non-stationarity, fouling, drift, and similar mechanisms are extracted
  outcomes, not membership criteria.
- The schema remains frozen at v2.2.1. Evidence-envelope normalization and
  page-list rules from `v2.2.1-frozen` remain in force.
- The superseded §13.2 n=30 pilot is not an execution target. Production and
  validation follow `VALIDATION_PROTOCOL_C.md` C-2.3 through independent clean
  Claude Code and Codex/ChatGPT application workspaces.

## Release delta

This release changes only this VERSION manifest so that the packaged prompt
metadata matches the already-tagged v2.3 Stage-1 content and the active C-2.3
workflow. `stage1_system.md`, `stage2_system.md`, and `stage3_system.md` are
byte-identical to `v2.3-eligibility-registered`.
